From eea76919e7160ea1797af7095d1d3657999d2f6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Anes <david.anes@suse.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:30:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Build configure.ac with autoconf 2.69

SLE-15 and SLE-12 ship autoconf 2.69, but configure.ac requires
2.71. Two changes are needed:
  * lower AC_PREREQ from 2.71 to 2.69
  * remove AC_CHECK_INCLUDES_DEFAULT (an autoconf 2.70+ macro)

The remaining macros used by configure.ac (AS_IF, AC_CHECK_TYPES,
AC_CHECK_FUNCS, AC_CHECK_MEMBERS, AC_USE_SYSTEM_EXTENSIONS, ...) are
all available in autoconf 2.69.
---
 configure.ac | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index d8621ca..f910913 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -8,3 +8,3 @@
 dnl a configure script.
-AC_PREREQ([2.71])
+AC_PREREQ([2.69])
 AC_INIT
@@ -56,7 +56,6 @@ dnl Check now to declare noreturn functions
 PA_C_NORETURN
 
 dnl Checks for header files.
-AC_CHECK_INCLUDES_DEFAULT
 
 dnl See if we need extra libraries
 XTRA=false
-- 
2.56.0
